    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:173cf987634ed90a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "fd8fb19b8577c772d1284f15026451546fcb6e4acbac8f37356abffde767c75b",
      "text": "After an early breakfast, get ready for the hike. We recommend comfortable shoes, a waterproof poncho, a jacket, sunscreen, water and a hat. Bring extra rain protection for your camera.\n\nThe bus or minibus ride to the national park checkpoint takes about 35 minutes. The checkpoint is roughly 22 km from Puerto Villamil.\n\nThe hike to Sierra Negra Volcano starts here. Allow about two hours for the round trip of 3–4 km. The steady, moderate incline makes this a moderately challenging hike. Horseback riding is available at an extra cost.\n\nSierra Negra’s crater is often described as the second largest in the world. It is about 9 km across and 100 m deep.\n\nBack at the hotel, you’ll have a short break. Then you can pick up snorkelling gear and head to Concha Perla Bay. Colourful fish, sea urchins, sea lions and sea turtles live in its clear waters.\n\nThe evening is free.\n\n**Accommodation:** Iguana Crossing, 4-star, Ocean View Room.  \n**Meals:** breakfast and a boxed lunch.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw8vsjy6-afdp41bp",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    },
